---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TermWindow from '../components/TermWindow.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Submit a server"
  description="How to add an MCP server to mcps.gallery: one YAML file, one pull request."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/" class="back">&larr; all servers</a>

      <TermWindow path="~/mcps.gallery/submit">
        <div class="layout">
          <div class="main">
            <h1 class="glow">submit a server</h1>
            <p class="lede">
              There's no submission form. This whole site is one file per server, and adding
              a listing means opening a pull request against the
              <a href="https://github.com/ThomasArdal/mcps.gallery" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThomasArdal/mcps.gallery</a>
              repository on GitHub.
            </p>

            <h2 id="add-yaml-file">1. add a yaml file</h2>
            <p>
              Copy <code>.github/server-listing-template.yml</code> into
              <code>src/data/servers/</code>, name it after your server (for example
              <code>my-server.yml</code>), and fill in the fields. That filename becomes the
              server's URL, so keep it short and lowercase with hyphens.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
              <pre><code>{`name: My Server
summary: One sentence, under 160 characters, no trailing period.
description: |
  A longer explanation, one or more paragraphs separated by a blank line.
  Plain text only, no markdown formatting.
repoUrl: https://github.com/you/my-server
homepageUrl: https://example.com          # optional
author: Your name or org
license: MIT                              # optional
language: TypeScript
transports: [stdio]                       # stdio, sse, and/or http
tags: [databases, developer-tools]
official: false
featured: false
installCommand: npx -y my-server           # optional
installConfig: |                           # optional
  {
    "mcpServers": {
      "my-server": {
        "command": "npx",
        "args": ["-y", "my-server"]
      }
    }
  }`}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <h2 id="check-locally">2. check it locally</h2>
            <p>
              Run <code>npm install && npm run build</code>. The build validates every
              listing against the schema in <code>src/content.config.ts</code> and fails
              with a clear error if a field is missing or the wrong type.
            </p>

            <h2 id="open-pr">3. open a pull request</h2>
            <p>
              Fork <a href="https://github.com/ThomasArdal/mcps.gallery" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">the repository</a>,
              push your change, and open a pull request against <code>main</code>.
              One server per pull request keeps review fast. The PR template asks two
              things: that the server is real and that you're not the sole judge of your
              own "official" claim. Mark <code>official: true</code> only if you maintain
              the underlying product, not just the MCP server for it.
            </p>

            <h2 id="rejected">what gets rejected</h2>
            <p>
              Servers that don't implement the Model Context Protocol, listings for a
              product rather than a server, and duplicates of an existing listing for the
              same repository.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="side">
            <h2>on this page</h2>
            <nav class="toc">
              <a href="#add-yaml-file">[1] add a yaml file</a>
              <a href="#check-locally">[2] check it locally</a>
              <a href="#open-pr">[3] open a pull request</a>
              <a href="#rejected">[#] what gets rejected</a>
            </nav>

            <h2>files</h2>
            <ul class="filelist">
              <li>.github/server-listing-template.yml</li>
              <li>src/data/servers/*.yml</li>
              <li>CONTRIBUTING.md</li>
            </ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </TermWindow>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: 40px 72px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .back:hover {
    color: var(--phosphor);
  }

  .layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 260px;
  }

  .main {
    padding: 36px 40px 48px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .side {
    padding: 36px 28px 44px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .side h2 {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .side h2:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .toc {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .toc a {
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .toc a:hover {
    color: var(--phosphor);
  }

  .filelist {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-top: 32px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--phosphor);
  }

  p {
    margin-top: 10px;
    max-width: 66ch;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .code-block {
    margin-top: 16px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .code-block pre {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .code-block code {
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .side {
      border-left: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
  }
</style>
